\n## Files to modify\n\n- `.goreleaser.yaml` — both `homebrew_casks` entries (`entire`, `entire@nightly`)\n\n## Diff sketch\n\nFor each of the two casks, replace this block:\n\n```yaml\n    completions:\n      bash: \"completions/entire.bash\"\n      zsh: \"completions/entire.zsh\"\n      fish: \"completions/entire.fish\"\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```yaml\n    generate_completions_from_executable:\n      executable: entire\n      args:\n        - completion\n      shell_parameter_format: cobra\n      shells:\n        - bash\n        - zsh\n        - fish\n```\n\nLeave everything else (binaries, conflicts, repository, skip_upload, etc.) unchanged.\n\nUntouched and intentional:\n- `before.hooks: mise run completions` — still useful for local dev and as a sanity check that the binary's completion command works.\n- `archives.files: completions/*` — tarball/Scoop installers still get pre-generated completion files.\n- `mise-tasks/completions` script — unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Schema sanity:** `goreleaser check` (or `goreleaser release --snapshot --clean --skip=publish,announce,sign,notarize`) succeeds against the modified config — proves goreleaser parses the new block.\n2. **Snapshot inspection:** after a `--snapshot` run, look at the generated cask Ruby file in `dist/` (homebrew tap output). Confirm it now uses goreleaser's installer-time `generate_completions` Ruby block instead of static `bash_completion/zsh_completion/fish_completion` `stage_path` entries.\n3. **Live cask test (one-off, post-merge or in a release dry-run):**\n   - `brew install --cask <tap>/entire` against a snapshot tap.\n   - Verify `~/.zshrc` / `compinit` picks up `entire` completions (`compdef -p entire` shows a definition; tab-complete `entire <TAB>` lists subcommands).\n4. **Goreleaser version pin check:** confirm the goreleaser version used in CI is `>= v2.15`. If it isn't, bump it before merging — older versions will fail to parse `generate_completions_from_executable`.\n\n## Out of scop